      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Upon reviewing the \"Modular Solid-State Battery Cooling Architecture\" (MSSBCA) and the prior art database, I have found that the core strength of MSSBCA lies in its unique combination of detachable cooling modules that allow for custom cooling profiles according to the battery’s heat output. This modularity is not indicated in any prior art I've reviewed. To argue novelty, I suggest we emphasize this modularity and the novel design of the cooling interface, which leads to increased efficiency and a lower likelihood of overheating. For non-obviousness, we can argue that this customized adaptability to thermodynamic conditions was neither predictable nor suggested by the prior art. Before filing, I'd recommend a comprehensive review of the entire database to search for subtle similarities that we might have overlooked, ensuring we are fully prepared to defend the MSSBCA’s claim to novelty and non-obviousness.",
      "source": "target",
